  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $ (in degrees), we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{202}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{202}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={158}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\n- $-{202}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={518}^{∘}$\n\nThere are no answer choices larger than ${518}^{∘},$ so we can stop here.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{202}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{202}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{562}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{202}^{∘}-2\\cdot {360}^{∘}=-{922}^{∘}$\n\nThere are no answer choices smaller than $-{922}^{∘},$ so we can stop here.\n\nSo the correct answer is ${158}^{∘}.$",
